      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-11T18:51:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "do we really want to silently catch a remote exception here?  If the process we bind to is already dead... how should the caller notice and handle that? I am guessing the right thing is to return null.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "7ddbb84b005007b8b787e0df5a7d0aa9bdbe3775",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ddd08dbe_ab0b9cbb",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/ims/ImsServiceProxyCompat.java",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1098053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-11T21:49:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If linkToDeath throws a RemoteException, mBinder will not be alive and fail any subsequent calls to this class via checkBinderConnection() and throw an exception at that point. Since this is called during the constructor of ImsManager, I don\u0027t want to modify it to throw an exception.\n\nNot a good design at this point, will try to refactor in the future (this addition was just moving the init code out of ImsManager).",
      "parentUuid": "33ddf845_eb0ee60e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 41
      },
